
/*
QUERY NAME: Fall 2026 YouTube Video Links in Course Content

PURPOSE:
Identifies and extracts YouTube video URLs found within
Blackboard Learn course item descriptions for courses
matching the Fall 2026 naming convention.

The query searches course content for YouTube links,
identifies whether each URL is an embedded video or
a standard YouTube link, and returns the course and
content item associated with each URL.

DATA SOURCES:
1. CDM_LMS.COURSE
   Contains Blackboard course information, including
   course names, course numbers, and identifiers.

2. CDM_LMS.COURSE_ITEM
   Contains course content items and their descriptions,
   which may include YouTube hyperlinks or embed codes.

TABLE RELATIONSHIP:
- COURSE_ITEM.COURSE_ID = COURSE.ID
- An INNER JOIN connects each content item to its course.
- Only course items belonging to matching courses
  are included.

COMMON TABLE EXPRESSION (CTE):
youtube_items

The CTE identifies course content containing YouTube
URLs and extracts those URLs into individual records.

FIELDS EXTRACTED IN THE CTE:
- course_key           : Internal COURSE.ID identifier.
- course_id            : Course batch_uid from COURSE.STAGE.
- course_number        : Blackboard course number.
- course_name          : Blackboard course name.
- course_item_id       : Unique content item identifier.
- course_item_name     : Name of the content item.
- item_type            : Content item type.
- item_type_source_code: Original LMS item type code.
- description          : Content item description.
- raw_youtube_url      : YouTube URL extracted from the
                         description before cleanup.

YOUTUBE URL EXTRACTION:
The query uses three Snowflake functions:

1. COALESCE(ci.description, '')
   Replaces NULL descriptions with an empty string
   so the regular expression can process them.

2. REGEXP_SUBSTR_ALL()
   Searches the description and returns an array
   containing all matching YouTube URLs.

   Supported URL patterns include:
   - youtube.com/watch?v=
   - youtube.com/embed/
   - youtube.com/shorts/
   - youtu.be/

   The expression also supports:
   - http:// and https:// URLs
   - Protocol-relative URLs beginning with //
   - URLs containing the www. prefix

3. LATERAL FLATTEN()
   Expands the array of YouTube URLs into separate rows.

   Each matching URL becomes its own result row.

   For example:
   - One content item with one YouTube URL produces one row.
   - One content item with three YouTube URLs produces
     three rows.
   - Content items without matching URLs are excluded.

FILTERING CONDITIONS:
1. c.stage:batch_uid::string ILIKE '%2026_FA'
   Limits results to courses whose batch_uid ends
   with a value matching the specified Fall 2026 pattern.

   - The batch_uid is extracted from the COURSE.STAGE
     JSON field.
   - ::string converts the JSON value into text.
   - ILIKE performs case-insensitive matching.
   - % allows any characters before the pattern.
   - The underscore (_) is a single-character wildcard
     in Snowflake SQL, not a literal underscore.

   IMPORTANT:
   Unlike ILIKE '%2026_FA%', this pattern requires the
   matching value to appear at the END of the batch_uid.

2. c.row_deleted_time IS NULL
   Excludes courses marked as deleted.

3. ci.row_deleted_time IS NULL
   Excludes course content items marked as deleted.

FINAL SELECT:
Returns course information, content item information,
a YouTube URL classification, and a cleaned URL.

YOUTUBE TYPE CLASSIFICATION:
The CASE statement categorizes each extracted URL.

- Embedded YouTube Video:
  URLs containing youtube.com/embed/

- YouTube Link:
  All other matching YouTube URLs, including watch links,
  Shorts links, and youtu.be links.

IMPORTANT:
The classification identifies the URL format.
It does not verify whether a video is actually displayed
as an embedded player in Blackboard.

YOUTUBE URL CLEANUP:
The REPLACE() expression standardizes extracted URLs.

1. If a URL begins with //
   The query adds https: to create a complete URL.

   Example:
   //www.youtube.com/embed/abc123

   Becomes:
   https://www.youtube.com/embed/abc123

2. Converts HTML-encoded ampersands:
   &amp; becomes &

   This helps restore YouTube URLs containing multiple
   query-string parameters.

SORTING:
Results are ordered by:
1. course_id        - Course batch UID, ascending.
2. course_item_name - Content item name, ascending.
3. youtube_url      - Extracted URL, ascending.

IMPORTANT NOTES:
- Only URLs found in COURSE_ITEM.DESCRIPTION are searched.
- YouTube URLs stored in other fields are not included.
- A content item can produce multiple rows when multiple
  YouTube URLs are present.
- Duplicate occurrences of the same URL are not removed.
- The query does not check whether courses or content
  items are available or enabled.
- The query does not verify whether a YouTube video
  is accessible, public, private, or deleted.
- The course_id output represents the batch_uid extracted
  from COURSE.STAGE, not COURSE.ID.
- The query uses the batch_uid naming convention to
  identify Fall 2026 courses rather than the TERM table.
- The regular expression may capture trailing URL
  punctuation or HTML entities beyond &amp;.
- Results represent discovered YouTube URL references,
  not video views, clicks, or student engagement.

*/

WITH youtube_items AS (
    SELECT
        c.id AS course_key,
        c.stage:batch_uid::string AS course_id,
        c.course_number,
        c.name AS course_name,

        ci.id AS course_item_id,
        ci.name AS course_item_name,
        ci.item_type,
        ci.item_type_source_code,
        ci.description,

        f.value::string AS raw_youtube_url

    FROM CDM_LMS.COURSE c

    INNER JOIN CDM_LMS.COURSE_ITEM ci
        ON ci.course_id = c.id

    , LATERAL FLATTEN(
        INPUT => REGEXP_SUBSTR_ALL(
            COALESCE(ci.description, ''),
            '(https?:)?//(www\\.)?(youtube\\.com/(watch\\?v=|embed/|shorts/)|youtu\\.be/)[^"''< >]+'
        )
    ) f

    WHERE c.stage:batch_uid::string ILIKE '%2026_FA'
      AND c.row_deleted_time IS NULL
      AND ci.row_deleted_time IS NULL
)

SELECT
    course_id,
    course_number,
    course_name,
    course_item_id,
    course_item_name,
    item_type,
    item_type_source_code,

    CASE
        WHEN LOWER(raw_youtube_url) LIKE '%youtube.com/embed/%'
            THEN 'Embedded YouTube Video'
        ELSE 'YouTube Link'
    END AS youtube_type,

    REPLACE(
        CASE
            WHEN raw_youtube_url LIKE '//%'
                THEN 'https:' || raw_youtube_url
            ELSE raw_youtube_url
        END,
        '&amp;',
        '&'
    ) AS youtube_url

FROM youtube_items

ORDER BY
    course_id,
    course_item_name,
    youtube_url;
